<title>GERMANY: Deutsche-no comment on Horlick flying to Frankfurt.</title>
<headline>Deutsche-no comment on Horlick flying to Frankfurt.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deutsche Bank AG on Friday declined immediate comment on a plan by Nicola Horlick, former head of the British pension fund business at Deutsche Morgan Grenfell's Morgan Grenfell Asset Management, to travel to Frankfurt to meet the bank's management board.</p>
<p>&quot;We can't make a statement on that yet,&quot; a Deutsche spokesman said in response to a Reuter enquiry.</p>
<p>Horlick told the BBC's &quot;Working Lunch&quot; television programme that she had requested the meeting, adding that allegations she had tried to get a job with a rival firm, which led to her suspension last week, were &quot;absolutely untrue,&quot; and that she had received &quot;very unfair treatment&quot; from MGAM.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
